statement:
Let m ∈ ℕ, n := m + 1, ρ > 0, and β : LatticeFaceIndex n n → ℝ with β_F ∈ ℤ for every F and Σ'_F ofReal(|β_F| ρ^n) < ∞. Then there are Pc ∈ D_n(ℝ^n) and v : ℝ^n → ℝ such that:
- IsLatticeChain ρ β Pc holds, i.e. Pc(ω) = Σ'_F β_F · latticeFaceAction ρ F ω for all ω;
- Pc is integer multiplicity;
- v is Lebesgue integrable;
- for every F, v = β_F a.e. on latticeFace ρ F;
- Pc(ω) = ∫ v(x) ω(x)(e_0, …, e_m) dx for every ω ∈ D^n(ℝ^n), where e_i = EuclideanSpace.single i 1.
